            <title>[LU-21312] Reserve one opcode in enum ost_cmd for an internal message channel between an MDS and an OSS</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21312</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Reserve one opcode in &lt;tt&gt;enum ost_cmd&lt;/tt&gt; for an internal message channel between an MDS and an OSS:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-c"&gt;
OST_MDS_MSG = 24
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The opcode is reserved for external services that run on MDS and OSS nodes and need their own data exchange, including vendor-specific services. Apart from a magic at the start of the request buffer, Lustre does not define the content of these messages, and no in-tree user is planned as part of this reservation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Properties:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Requests are sent only by an MDS (&lt;tt&gt;OBD_CONNECT_MDS&lt;/tt&gt; export) to an OST. Data from the OSS travels back in the reply. Clients do not use this opcode.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The request carries one buffer after &lt;tt&gt;ptlrpc_body&lt;/tt&gt; that ptlrpc does not parse. Its first &lt;tt&gt;__u32&lt;/tt&gt; is a magic chosen by the service owner, so that several services can share the opcode and a receiver can reject a message that is not meant for it. The rest of the buffer is defined by the service.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A server with no handler for the opcode answers &lt;tt&gt;-EOPNOTSUPP&lt;/tt&gt;. This relies on &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19916" title="FTM: start MGS replicas on MDTs/OSTs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19916"&gt;LU-19916&lt;/a&gt; ("target: size handler tables to their opcode range"); without it an OSS or MDT reads past the end of its OST handler table for this opcode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
